From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 17:16:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fire the Bukkit portal and teleport events for a vanilla
 portal

Folia rewrote Entity#handlePortal to call portalProcess.portalAsync instead of
getPortalDestination() + teleport(transition). That reroute drops every Bukkit
event a portal used to fire, because both of the places they were fired from are
now dead code:

  - Portal#getPortalDestination, where CraftEventFactory.handlePortalEvents
    fires PlayerPortalEvent and EntityPortalEvent, has no live caller left. Both
    events are dead API on this fork.
  - ServerPlayer#teleport(TeleportTransition), where PlayerTeleportEvent is
    fired, is an unconditional throw, and portalToAsync reaches placeInAsync
    without ever going through teleportAsync - so it never reaches the hook that
    restores that event either.

Measured, not argued, with the same probe and the same Multiverse-Core 5.7.2 on
both platforms, world.enforce-access true, a player without
multiverse.access.world_nether walking into a nether portal:

  Paper     portal-LOWEST NETHER_PORTAL cancelled=false
            Multiverse: Failure{reason=NO_WORLD_ACCESS}
            portal-MONITOR cancelled=true          -> player stays in world
  this fork no portal event, no teleport event      -> player is in world_nether

Every other teleport path already matched Paper in the same run - the plugin API,
the sync API, /mv tp from the player and from the console all fired the event and
all honoured the cancel on both platforms. The portal is the only hole, and it is
the way players actually change world.

Fired from portalToAsync, after canPortalAsync and Luminol's PreEntityPortalEvent
and before the unload lock, the passenger detach and the transform: the same four
properties the teleportAsync hook relies on. teleportAsync opens with
ensureTickThread, so the handler runs on the region that owns the entity; nothing
is mutated yet, so a cancel is a plain return false, the answer portalToAsync
already gives for its own refusals; it is above the nether/end split; and no lock
is held, so a cancel cannot leak one.

Cancellation, setTo, setSearchRadius, setCreationRadius and setCanCreatePortal
are all honoured - the last three are passed into the platform's own asynchronous
portal search. PlayerPortalEvent's to is the approximate scaled exit, which is
exactly what Paper passes it, so that event is at parity. PlayerTeleportEvent's
to is that same approximate exit rather than the resolved portal exit, because
the search completes on another region after the entity has been detached and
transformed, where a cancel could not be honoured without unwinding a half
finished handover. World, cause and cancellation are exact; the position can be
off by up to the portal search radius.

Kill switch: event-config.portal-events=false.

